@using EchoLifestyle.Application.Administration.CompanyProfile
@model CompanyDetail
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] =
        "What Echo Lifestyle collects, why, and who it is shared with.";
}

<div class="container py-4 py-lg-5">
    <div class="shop-prose mx-auto">

        <h1 class="shop-display h2">Privacy</h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            Short version: we keep what we need to deliver your order, we give the courier
            what they need to find you, and we sell your details to nobody.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>

        <p>When you place an order we keep:</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Your name and the name the parcel is going to.</li>
            <li>Your phone number. This is how we confirm orders and how the courier
                reaches you, and it is how we recognise you next time.</li>
            <li>The delivery address, and any note you leave with it.</li>
            <li>What you ordered and what it cost.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            You do not need an account to shop with us, and we do not ask for one. We do
            not collect your date of birth, your national ID, or any payment card details
            &mdash; there is nothing to collect, because you pay the courier in cash.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees it</h2>

        <p>
            The courier delivering your parcel gets your name, phone number and address.
            They need all three to deliver it, and nothing beyond that.
        </p>

        <p>
            Nobody else gets your name, number or address. We do not sell, rent or trade
            customer details.
        </p>

        <h2>The basket</h2>

        <p>
            Your basket is remembered with a small cookie that holds nothing but a random
            identifier. It is not tied to you until you place an order, and it expires by
            itself after two weeks.
        </p>

        @* Written because the site actually does this, and a privacy page that
           did not mention it would be false. If the tracking ids are ever
           cleared in Administration this section stops being true - hence the
           condition rather than a paragraph that is always printed. *@
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.MetaPixelId)
             || !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.GoogleAnalyticsId))
        {
            <h2>Measuring the website</h2>

            <p>
                We advertise on Facebook and Instagram, and we need to know which of those
                adverts actually lead to orders &mdash; otherwise we are spending money
                blind. So this website reports anonymous activity to
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.MetaPixelId)
                     && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.GoogleAnalyticsId))
                {
                    <text>Meta (Facebook) and Google Analytics</text>
                }
                else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.MetaPixelId))
                {
                    <text>Meta (Facebook)</text>
                }
                else
                {
                    <text>Google Analytics</text>
                }:
                which pages were viewed, what was added to a basket, and the value of an
                order once it is placed.
            </p>

            <p>
                <strong>Your name, phone number and address are never sent to them.</strong>
                What they receive is page activity and order values, tied to a browser
                rather than to a person by us. These companies do their own tracking across
                the web, which is outside our control &mdash; a browser set to block
                trackers, or an ad-blocker, stops this and does not affect your ability to
                order.
            </p>
        }

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>

        <p>
            Order records are kept as long as we are required to keep business records,
            and because they are how we answer questions about past orders and honour
            anything that turns out to be our fault.
        </p>

        <h2>Asking us to change or remove something</h2>

        <p>
            Message or call us and we will correct anything that is wrong. If you want us
            to stop contacting you, say so and we will. We cannot delete the record of an
            order that has already been placed and delivered, because that is an accounting
            record, but nothing obliges us to keep contacting you about it.
        </p>

        <h2>Getting hold of us</h2>

        <p>
            @Model.Name@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Phone) ? "" : $", {Model.Phone}")@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.Email) ? "" : $", {Model.Email}").
            Details are on the <a asp-route="storefront-contact">contact page</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="text-muted small">
            We will update this page if what we do changes. It is written to describe what
            the shop actually does rather than to cover every eventuality, which is the
            only kind of privacy notice worth reading.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
